# Generated artifacts — regenerated deterministically by the pipeline
# (src/generate_data.py uses a fixed SEED and start date, so every run is identical).
# (data/raw is ~8 MB of synthetic events; CI regenerates it from the seed.)
data/raw/*.csv
data/quality/*
data/marts/*
output/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/quality/.gitkeep
!data/marts/.gitkeep
!output/.gitkeep

# ...with two deliberate exceptions, versioned so the repo is self-demonstrating:
#
# 1. data/marts/*.csv — daily_fpy.csv and station_scorecard.csv are the CSVs
#    written by the PySpark job on Databricks (workspace.quality.daily_fpy /
#    .station_scorecard), kept as provenance for the published pages.
#    pareto.csv comes from the local validation stage; Spark does not emit it.
#    Running `python -m src.pipeline_pandas` locally overwrites them with the
#    pandas run: identical values, slightly different float formatting, so
#    git may show them as modified. That is expected — the two implementations
#    are diffed cell-for-cell and agree to 4.44e-16.
# 2. output/*.html — the scorecard and dashboard are served by GitHub Pages,
#    so they must be committed rather than built on demand.
!data/marts/*.csv
!output/*.html

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
